WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.949
Every ticket names an asset,

2
00:00:01.949 --> 00:00:06.325
so the help desk can only be as
right as the inventory it routes to.

3
00:00:06.325 --> 00:00:09.985
The configuration database
earns that trust by agreeing

4
00:00:09.985 --> 00:00:13.112
with one authoritative
identity, not by being one.

5
00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:17.751
Discovery fills it in; the naming and
addressing record governs identity.

6
00:00:17.751 --> 00:00:22.912
Where the two disagree, the database is
wrong, and the disagreement is a finding.

7
00:00:22.912 --> 00:00:25.657
ServiceNow already prevents duplicates and

8
00:00:25.657 --> 00:00:28.400
controls which source
writes each attribute.

9
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:33.864
The program adds one pass: match each
asset to the naming record, bind it, and

10
00:00:33.864 --> 00:00:39.687
flag the rest, either a shadow asset nobody
approved or a gap to fix at the source.

11
00:00:39.687 --> 00:00:42.237
Duplicates are resolved by binding,

12
00:00:42.237 --> 00:00:45.550
not deleting, so no open
finding loses its asset.

13
00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:50.438
Otherwise a fix can land on one copy
while the finding stays open on the other.

14
00:00:50.438 --> 00:00:53.620
Next, automating the
controls in each cloud.
